From 190fb75d518dd86bc8a44159fa48bc98a173dc0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nassos Yiannopoulos <nassosyian@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:52:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/54] hw/display/pvg-linux-pci: task mappings, object table,
 backing scanout, Metal stream parser

MapMemory2/UnmapMemory keep host-side page snapshots per task;
SetObjectList records each task's object table; Transaction3 resolves the
presented surface (a BGRA Backing object) and copies it into the console.
ExecIndirect2 command buffers are read from user task memory, split into
encoder segments, traced, and optionally dumped (dump-dir) for analysis.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
